# Rule 100100 false positives — observed live

Edge updated itself at 13:19 and generated 5 alerts in 22 seconds:
- Run\MicrosoftEdgeAutoLaunch_...
- RunOnce\Delete Cached Update Binary
- RunOnce\Delete Cached Standalone Update Binary
- RunOnce\Uninstall 26.134.0713.0007  (x2)

Predicted this yesterday — wrote that 1 event/24h reflected an
idle box, not a tight rule. Confirmed within 24 hours.

Also: 4 of 5 were RunOnce, not Run. My rule matches "CurrentVersion"
AND "Run" as separate conditions, and "RunOnce" contains "Run".
Catching RunOnce by accident.

DECISION: keeping RunOnce coverage. Both Run and RunOnce are valid
persistence locations under T1547.001. Rule covers both intentionally.
